    "result_text": "All 256 tests pass, including the new `AcceptanceTest.coreComputesInitials`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds an `initials` field to the owner API response, computed as the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `\"J.S.\"`).\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema. This drives the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto`, which is what the REST controllers return.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Wired the new field into the MapStruct mapping via `@Mapping(target = \"initials\", ...)`, alongside the existing `displayName` handling. Added a `formatInitials(owner)` helper and an `initial(name)` helper that upper-cases the first character and appends a dot (null/empty-safe).\n\nThe implementation follows the existing `displayName` pattern in the same mapper, so it fits the established Spring/MapStruct conventions in the codebase. The full test suite is green (256 tests, 0 failures).",
